.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH tix-completions 1  "completions " 
.SH NAME
tix\-completions \- Generate shell completions (top\-level alias for `tix cli completions`)
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBtix completions\fR [\fB\-\-config\fR] [\fB\-o\fR|\fB\-\-output\fR] [\fB\-\-log\-level\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fISHELL\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Generate shell completions (top\-level alias for `tix cli completions`)
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-config\fR \fI<CONFIG>\fR
Path to the global config file (overrides TIX_CONFIG_PATH and the platform default)
.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-output\fR \fI<OUTPUT>\fR
Output format for commands that support it (also forwarded to plugins as \-\-tix\-output)
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
json
.IP \(bu 2
toml
.IP \(bu 2
default
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-log\-level\fR \fI<LOG_LEVEL>\fR
Set the log level (trace, debug, info, warn, error)
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Set the log level to trace (shorthand for \-\-log\-level trace)
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Set the log level to warn (shorthand for \-\-log\-level warn)
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fISHELL\fR>
The shell to generate completions for
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
bash
.IP \(bu 2
elvish
.IP \(bu 2
fish
.IP \(bu 2
powershell
.IP \(bu 2
zsh
.RE
.SH EXTRA
Installation:
  bash:        tix completions bash > /etc/bash_completion.d/tix
               (or: ~/.local/share/bash\-completion/completions/tix)
  zsh:         tix completions zsh > ~/.zfunc/_tix
               (with `fpath+=~/.zfunc; autoload \-Uz compinit; compinit` in ~/.zshrc)
  fish:        tix completions fish > ~/.config/fish/completions/tix.fish
  elvish:      tix completions elvish > ~/.config/elvish/lib/tix.elv
  powershell:  tix completions powershell >> $PROFILE
